We prove a simple sufficient criteria to obtain some Hardy inequalities on Riemannian manifolds related to quasilinear second-order differential operator $\Delta_{p}u := \Div(\abs{
abla u}^{p-2}
abla u)$. Namely, if $ho$ is a nonnegative weight such that $-\Delta_{p}ho\geq0$, then the Hardy inequality $$c\int_{M} rac{\abs{u}^{p}}{ho^{p}}\abs{
abla ho}^{p} dv_{g} \leq \int_{M}\abs{
abla u}^{p} dv_{g}, \quad u\in\Cinfinito_{0}(M)$$ holds. We show concrete examples specializing the function $ho$.

Recently, several bounds have been obtained on the number of solutions to congruences of the type $$ (x_1+s)...(x_{
u}+s)\equiv (y_1+s)...(y_{
u}+s)
ot\equiv0 \pmod p $$ modulo a prime $p$ with variables from some short intervals. Here, for almost all $p$ and all $s$ and also for a fixed $p$ and almost all $s$, we derive stronger bounds. We also use similar ideas to show that for almost all primes, one can always find an element of a large order in any rather short interval.
